// G is false (the play leaves {p} every other step) but G F is true (it returns to p
// every other step, forever) -- the minimal distinguishing case for the Buchi
// construction, checked here for sure mode and, since there's no adversary or
// probability, almost/limit agree too (a regression check on the collapse for a genuinely
// cyclic, not just settling, model).

// RESULT: false
<<p1>> sure [ G x=0 ]

// RESULT: true
<<p1>> sure [ G F x=0 ]

// RESULT: true
<<p1>> almost [ G F x=0 ]

// RESULT: true
<<p1>> limit [ G F x=0 ]
